10.16.080
Citation on illegally parked vehicles.
Whenever any motor vehicle without a driver is found parked, standing or stopped in
violation of any of the restrictions imposed by ordinances of this city or by state law, the officer
finding the vehicle shall take its registration number, vehicle identification number or any other
information displayed on the vehicle which may identify its owner, and shall conspicuously affix
to the vehicle a civil traffic citation.A violation underthis section, Chapter(s)10.52,10.56,10.60
504(a)(i)(A) and 10.64.020 shall constitute a civil traffic violation, subject to civil sanctions
as provided here in.
