10.60.010Signed time limitations.
Vehicles parked in an area where parking is limited by time must move one hundred fifty
(150)fcetfrom the block face of thevehicle'sparked position before the expiration of time
indicated on posted signs onany dayexcept Sundays and public holidays, unless otherwise indicated
upon any of the streets within the city as designated by the city traffic engineer.
“Block face” is defined as one side of a specific city block where signed time limited
parking is available.
10.60.030
Notice of violation.
When a vehicle is found to be in violation of this chapter a notice specifying the violation
and amount of the fine will be affixed to thevehicle, or sent to the address indicated by current
license plate registration records to the registered ownerof thevehicle.
The notice of violation will also indicate the manner in which the citation may be
contested. time and place of court appearance.  The violation(s) may be paid in the manner
indicated on the notice in lieu of a court appearance.
